  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 256 AM EDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\n- Blocking Pattern Brings Fair Weather \n\nTHe sharp upper trough that brought the cold air and lake effect\nshowers moves east over the weekend with rising heights and \nsouthwest flow bringing warmer temperatures. However, the current \ncold airmass will still be in place for tonight and another round \nof frost/freeze conditions can be expected away from Lake Michigan\nwhere winds can decouple. The growing season will be ended on \nSunday, since we are past the climatological end of the season and\nthe two nights of cold temperatures.\n\nNo precipitation is expected for the next week under upper\nridging. Height falls may finally happen next weekend as a\nshortwave trough moves across southern Canada and approaches the\nGreat Lakes.",
